  "id": "COMPOUND:16022 - PROTEIN:6156",
  "verbalization": "Dalbergichromene is shown to interact with G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1 through multiple pathways, with the most direct evidence linking it to the enzyme Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta. This enzyme is targeted by both Dalbergichromene and Maytansine, a well-documented anticancer compound, which in turn binds to G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1. The presence of multiple independent targets—Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta and 13-Demethyldysidenin—suggests a broader mechanism of action, potentially involving the regulation of cyclin B1 expression or activity. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically plausible relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The involvement of splicing factors and cyclin B1 highlights the complexity of the pathway, with Dalbergichromene potentially modulating cellular processes critical for mitosis.",
